From dca1d7a8efa655d1796cc998eb81573817716c1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:29:52 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Sun shadows: Wind Waker HD's caster culling and lava glow in
 its lit rooms (aurora_set_sun_caster_cull)

HD draws its shadow map's casters with their materials' cull mode (an HD capture of
Dragon Roost Cavern's room 0: 225 of its 240 map draws cull back faces, the
rest none), with its bias (80, 3) for the faces that do cast. RecompCore drew
every caster's both sides, so in a closed room the ceiling, seen from the room
light above, shaded the whole floor.

aurora_set_sun_caster_cull(on): the scenery's casters take their draw's own cull
mode (DrawData::sunCasterCull, front face clockwise as the scene's pipelines);
characters keep their own (none, or DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_CHARACTER_CULL).
DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_CASTER_CULL=1 or 0 overrides the host for tests. The host
turns it on in HD's lit rooms only; outdoors keeps both sides until it is
checked there.

Wind Waker HD's lava glow in its lava and fire rooms (GanonB, Cave01, MiniKaz,
Ganon's Tower's lava parts). HD's lava materials (PS 4345 in Cemu) add albedo
x lava K x 4 x the vertex red squared to the light, outside the shade, with
lava K the material's konst2 animation at the game frame (GanonB's capture:
0.453, 0.0415, 0.0005, its frame 23). A version 2 stage table has that curve
and each vertex's glow; a lit room draw in the GameCube's two-stage form (the
light, then x the texture) takes it from its vertices' colour 1 after the last
stage, and their share of the lit light goes through the sea mask's pass into
the normals' alpha, which the sun pass leaves unshaded. Cave01 goes from 0.47
to 0.97 of HD's brightness and from HD's red (0.77 red share) to its hue
(0.50, HD 0.49); GanonB from 0.60 to 0.86.

Dragon Roost Cavern's lava glow. HD's shaders for its konst2 materials (the
disc's model.sharcfb) add albedo x lava K x 4 x (1 - the vertex alpha)
squared, which the importer now gives as the glow, by the same rule as
Ganon's Tower's. Its _v_x materials are three stages on the GameCube, a
third PREV + C1 x APREV (the GameCube's own glow), and HD's program for
each is its plain material's: no such term. hd_lava_shape takes that form,
the draw takes C1 black (hd_light_constants()), and the glow goes on after
stage 1, on its texel (emit_hd_lava(); stage 2 has none). Two-stage draws
make the same WGSL as before. Room 11's lit right wall goes from 0.71 of
HD's red to 1.02 (Cemu, 12:00).

The Tower of the Gods' water floor (Obj_Humi's Humi00_v, the only material of its kind on the disc) sums its colours
in linear light, as Wind Waker HD's shader for it does (Cemu, ToG room 0, PS 27623): KONST + C0 x texel, plus
KONST x the second layer's texel x (1 - the vertex alpha x the first's), on the colours made linear in 8 bits
((c / 255)^2.2, HD's constants 4,11,10 and 11,28,27 for the game's 39,61,59 and 61,93,92), then back to gamma for the
GX fog. On the GameCube's gamma colours the caustics came out twice HD's brightness in linear. gxc::
hd_water_floor_stage() matches its three stages; ShaderKey::hd_water (the pad byte) flags it while HD's palettes are
in place (post_fx::actor_light_wanted()). HD's (1 + light buffer) / 2 is 1 where the floor is lit and is left to the
sun pass. WGSL test: the match, its rejects and the block's place.

ToG room 0 at 12:00, 16 frames: the floor's linear luminance 0.155 -> 0.098 (Cemu 0.074); the lit caustics
0.223 -> 0.120 (Cemu about 0.10), the floor colour itself unchanged. The rest is the boat's ripple quads.
ToG room 1, the sea and Cave01 are unchanged (no draw of the shape there).
